78 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406962 13194139533526 17592186045585 true] [17592186406978 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406964 13194139533526 17592186045585 true] [17592186406978 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406967 13194139533526 17592186045585 true] [17592186406978 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406972 13194139533526 17592186045585 true] [17592186406978 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533526 17592186045585 true] [17592186406978 1077 "selection" 13194139533526 17592186045585 true] [17592186406978 1079 #edb/ref 17592186406964 13194139533526 17592186045585 true] [17592186406978 1080 #uuid "6a77f2d5-b26b-5d52-b3a8-7c324acb6f02" 13194139533526 17592186045585 true] [17592186406979 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406961 13194139533526 17592186045585 true] [17592186406979 1075 #edb/ref 17592186406971 13194139533526 17592186045585 true] [17592186406979 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139533526 17592186045585 true] [17592186406979 1077 "field-4" 13194139533526 17592186045585 true] [17592186406979 1079 #edb/ref 17592186406961 13194139533526 17592186045585 true] [17592186406979 1080 #uuid "b4032492-1493-553b-bc31-fe628a9c1050" 13194139533526 17592186045585 true] [17592186406980 1068 #edb/ref 17592186406978 13194139533526 17592186045585 true] [17592186406980 1069 "q-103558" 13194139533526 17592186045585 true] [17592186406980 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533526 17592186045585 true] [17592186406980 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- **If** $12$ is divisible by $3$, **then** $9$ is divisible by $4.$\n- **If** $5$ is divisible by $2$, **then** $10$ is divisible by $5.$\n- **If** $9$ is divisible by $5$, **then** $6$ is divisible by $3.$" 13194139533526 17592186045585 true] [17592186406980 1072 #uuid "55e540af-11e2-5ec3-9b47-ab0da3ac740e" 13194139533526 17592186045585 true] [17592186406980 1074 "An implication $A⇒B$ is true *unless* $A$ is true and $B$ is false. In other words, the implication is true unless the \"promise\" is broken.\n\n- Statement I is false. The antecedent \"$12$ is divisible by $3$\" is true, and the consequent \"$9$ is divisible by $4$\" is false. So the promise is broken, and the statement is false.\n\n- Statement II is true. The antecedent \"$5$ is divisible by $2$\" is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\n- Statement III is true. Again, the antecedent \"$9$ is divisible by $5$\" is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139533526 17592186045585 true] [17592186406981 1068 #edb/ref 17592186406974 13194139533526 17592186045585 true] [17592186406981 1069 "q-82092" 13194139533526 17592186045585 true] [17592186406981 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533526 17592186045585 true] [17592186406981 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- **If** $7$ is an even number, **then** $6$ is an odd number.\n- **If** $6$ is an even number, **then** $7$ is an even number.\n- **If** $6$ is an even number, **then** $7$ is an odd number." 13194139533526 17592186045585 true] [17592186406981 1072 #uuid "806aafe6-aa9d-53f3-a7d9-19809d388a29" 13194139533526 17592186045585 true] [17592186406981 1074 "An implication $A⇒B$ is true *unless* $A$ is true and $B$ is false. In other words, the implication is true unless the \"promise\" is broken.\n\n- Statement I is true. The antecedent \"$7$ is an even number\" is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\n- Statement II is false. The antecedent \"$6$ is an even number\" is true, and the consequent \"$7$ is an even number\" is false. So the promise is broken, and the statement is false.\n\n- Statement III is true. The antecedent \"$6$ is an even number\" is true, and the consequent \"$7$ is an odd number\" is true. So the promise is kept, and the statement is true.\n\nTherefo